An app in Latvian (in the future English as well) probably a web app, that can be hosted by each user so there is no public server. Peer to peer can be an option, probably a good one.
App tracks kids points that are gathered doing overall good deeds:
* cleaning the house
* dishes / clothes
* looking after siblings
* being overy polite
* etc

git repo: https://github.com/rihardiii/punktu_sistema.git

[x] starting version 0.01
[x] version increment by .01 or more depending on how big of a change or addition
[x] Each good deed has some weight to it and good deeds can be added in the future by the parents.
[x] Each good deed should have some icon representing it (can be generated or added by the user or left blank)
[x] multiple users: Mom, Dad and a Kid.
[x] Mom and Dad are parent / admin users
[x] kid is normal users
[x] parents can have multiple kids
[x] app can be used in android and windows and linux (optional)
[x] kid can add newly done job and parents can after inspection accept it and the points can be added to the kids account
[x] points can be exchanged to other stuff by the kid, for example: console playtime, money and so on
[x] parents accept or deny the request.
[x] dark / light / custom
[x] kids friendly design
[x] friendly to parents as well
[x] adding a new family member: when typing in the name / username / pin it automatically deselects the text box after one keypress on windoes brave browser (havent tested on others)
