[x] add open source licence — MIT. Note: "free to use but not distribute, no
    commercial use" is not open source; no OSI licence allows it. MIT was chosen
    because README and package.json already declared it. To actually forbid
    commercial use later, swap LICENSE for PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0.
[x] fix other stuff if there are any
    - security headers (CSP, nosniff, referrer policy)
    - production sourcemaps dropped (~1.7 MB off every image and phone precache)

[x] make the GHCR package public — docs and stack file now assume a public
    package: the docker login / token / manual pull dance is gone, and Dockge's
    Update button is the whole update story. Also dropped the "copy the folder
    to the NAS" path (deploy/standalone), which only existed to avoid tokens.

Jādara pašam / do this yourself (cannot be done from here):
[x] GitHub -> repo -> Packages -> punktu_sistema -> Package settings ->
    Change visibility -> Public. Until this is clicked, the NAS will get
    "denied / unauthorized" when it pulls the image.

[x] i am unable to edit existing tasks or prizes, when i try to edit and save it says invalid value
    - the form sent active back as the 0/1 a row carries; the server only took
      a JSON boolean. Fixed both ends, and the api types now forbid the mistake.
      Same bug also broke the Deactivate / Activate buttons.
[x] when editing the points text box always stays at least 1, which is annoying if i want to add 5 points, I have to place cursor in between 1 and 5 just to delete 5
    - the box now keeps what you type, may be empty, and Save stays disabled
      until there is a number in it
[x] add more generic icons in all of the categories — 12 -> 24 per group
[x] add health / bathroom categories for icons
[x] what about notifications?
    - in-app only: a count on the tab (parent: waiting for a decision, and
      forgotten PINs; kid: a request was answered) plus a toast on screen.
    - real push is not possible here: it needs an HTTPS certificate and a
      detour through Google's or Mozilla's servers, which is what self-hosting
      this was meant to avoid. Revisit only if the NAS ever gets HTTPS.
[x] deeds and rewards buttons are inline with the text but when it is in latvian the text is longer than the english version and it makes the buttons drop down.
    - the toggle now takes its own full-width row below the heading until the
      screen is wide enough for both (560px). Shared .page-head class.
[x] a timeframe for some tasks (for example brush your teeth can be done only in the morning and evening)
    - up to four windows per deed, because "morning and evening" is two ranges
      and one from/to pair could never say it. Enforced on the server too, not
      just greyed out on screen.
[x] how many times some tasks can be done (for example brushing teeth can be done twice, cleaning your room - once a day)
    - pending submissions count against the cap, rejected ones give the slot
      back. The day boundary is the server's (TZ=Europe/Riga), not the phone's.
[x] some sort of automatic update without page refresh?
    - every screen re-reads its data every 15s, pauses while the tab is hidden
      and catches up the moment it is looked at again.
[x] create a test.cmd that proposes to run tests:
0. All tests
1. Typecheck only
2. API tests
3. Browser tests
Default 0
i choose a test and run it.
so i can open the web page on localhost and test the new features after which i can ctrl+c to close it
    - test.cmd in the repo root. Double-click it, or `test.cmd 2` to skip the
      menu. Every choice ends by serving the app on localhost:4173 and opening
      the browser; Ctrl+C closes it.
    - the manual-test server uses data\test.sqlite, never the family's
      data\punkti.sqlite. Delete that file to start from an empty house.
    - if tests fail it says so and asks before serving anyway.
    - no version bump: this is tooling, the app itself did not change.
[x] add one place in main file or a constants file where the version number is located and references, so that it is edited in one place instead of 5
    - the one place is the root package.json "version" (semver). The server
      reads it at startup; Vite inlines it into the web bundle at build time;
      CI already read it for the image tag.
    - 0.12.0 -> "0.12" and 0.9.0 -> "0.09", matching the .01 scheme. Each side
      does that conversion itself, so ui.mjs checks the screen and /api/health
      agree, and smoke.sh checks both match package.json.
    - server/package.json and web/package.json no longer carry a version at
      all (private workspaces, nothing read them). docker-compose.yml builds
      locally and is now tagged :local instead of a version.
    - CHANGELOG still gets a new heading per release — that is a log, not a
      copy of the number.
    - to release 0.13: edit that one line. npm ci does not mind the lockfile
      being a version behind; `npm install --package-lock-only` syncs it.
[x] before we push a major version, each commit and push increments a minor version number 0.0.1 for example. major version is 0.1.0 and so on.
    - .githooks/pre-commit bumps the last digit on every commit: 0.12.1,
      0.12.2, ... For a release set the middle digit by hand (0.13.0) and the
      hook leaves it alone, because it only bumps when the version still
      matches HEAD.
    - it bumps once per commit, not per push: pushing five commits does not
      add five more.
    - skipped for merge / rebase / cherry-pick. `git commit --no-verify`
      skips it once.
    - the hook lives in the repo (not .git/hooks) so it travels with a clone;
      `npm install` points git at it via the "prepare" script. One-time
      manual equivalent: git config core.hooksPath .githooks
    - the UI shows 0.12.1 for a patch build and plain 0.13 for a release.
[x] about section that shows version shows only 0.12 instead of 0.12.1 as it should
    - cause: the web bundle baked the version in at build time, but every
      commit bumps it, so the number went stale the moment it was built and
      stayed stale until the next npm run build. A cached service-worker
      bundle could show it for longer still.
    - fix: the About screen now asks the server (/api/health), which reads the
      manifest at startup. /api is never cached, so it cannot go stale.
      Verified by bumping to 0.12.9 without rebuilding: the screen followed.
    - bonus: the 0.12.0 -> 0.12 conversion now exists in one place only
      (server/src/version.ts); the vite define and web/src/version.ts are gone.
    - if the server is unreachable the screen shows a dash, not an old number.
[x] browser test should only build and run in browser instead of running all the checks
    - new option 4 "Tikai uzbūvēt / Just build and open": builds and serves,
      no checks at all, ~15s to a usable app instead of ~2 min.
    - option 3 still runs the Playwright suite, so nothing was lost — 4 is the
      "I just want to look at it" path.
    - option 4 skips the pass/fail summary too, since nothing ran. If the
      build itself fails it still says so and asks before serving.